{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Regular"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.norm_one_sub_weierstrassFactor_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.norm_one_sub_weierstrassFactor_le","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L262-L315","doc":"**Weierstrass estimate.**  For `‖z‖ ≤ 1`, `‖1 - Eₚ(z)‖ ≤ ‖z‖^{p+1}`.\n\nThe constant is exactly `1` because the total mass\n`∫₀¹ t^p exp(Sₚ(t)) dt` equals `1 - Eₚ(1) = 1` on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.oneSub_weierstrassFactor_eq_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.oneSub_weierstrassFactor_eq_integral","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L245-L260","doc":"**Integral representation.**  `1 - Eₚ(z) = ∫₀¹ z^{p+1}·t^p·exp(Sₚ(tz)) dt`.\nImmediate from `hasDerivAt_weierstrassFactor` along the segment `t ↦ tz`,\nusing `Eₚ(0) = 1` at the lower endpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR_mono","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L221-L228","doc":"`Sₚ` is monotone in its (nonnegative) real argument, so shrinking `‖z‖`\nbelow `1` only shrinks the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.re_expSum_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.re_expSum_le","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L208-L219","doc":"`Re Sₚ(w) ≤ Sₚ(‖w‖)`: termwise, `Re(w^k) ≤ ‖w‖^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.integral_pow_mul_exp_expSumR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.integral_pow_mul_exp_expSumR","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L184-L204","doc":"**The total mass is exactly `1`.**  `∫₀¹ t^p·exp(Sₚ(t)) dt = 1`.\n\nThis is the sharp step.  Bounding the integrand crudely by `exp(H_p)`\nwould give `e^{H_p}/(p+1) > 1` for `p ≥ 1` — too weak.  Here the integral\nis evaluated EXACTLY by the fundamental theorem of calculus applied to\n`1 - Eₚ`, whose endpoint values are `0` and `1 - Eₚ(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR_one","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L179-L182","doc":"**`Eₚ(1) = 0` on ℝ.**  This single value is what makes the main constant\nexactly `1`: the total mass of the integral below is `1 - Eₚ(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR_zero","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L176-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR_zero","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L173-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_weierstrassFactorR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_weierstrassFactorR","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L156-L171","doc":"Real analogue of the derivative identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_expSumR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_expSumR","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L139-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactorR","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L135-L137","doc":"Real primary factor `Eₚ(t) = (1-t)·exp(Sₚ(t))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSumR","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L131-L133","doc":"Real exponent polynomial `Sₚ(t) = ∑_{k=1}^{p} t^k/k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_weierstrassFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_weierstrassFactor","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L104-L127","doc":"**`Eₚ'(z) = -z^p · exp(Sₚ(z))`.**\n\nThe telescoping `(1 - z)·∑_{k<p} z^k = 1 - z^p` is the whole content: it\ncancels the `-1` coming from differentiating the linear factor, leaving a\nsingle monomial `-z^p`.  This is why `Eₚ` is \"flat to order `p`\" at the\norigin and hence why the canonical product converges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_expSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.hasDerivAt_expSum","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L80-L102","doc":"`Sₚ` is differentiable, with `Sₚ'(z) = ∑_{k<p} z^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor_one","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**`Eₚ(1) = 0`.**  The linear factor vanishes at `1`; this is what makes the\nconstant in the main estimate exactly `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor_apply_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor_apply_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L68-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L63-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.weierstrassFactor","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The **Weierstrass primary factor** `Eₚ(z) = (1 - z)·exp(Sₚ(z))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WeierstrassFactorEstimate.expSum","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WeierstrassFactorEstimate.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The exponent polynomial `Sₚ(z) = ∑_{k=1}^{p} z^k/k`, reindexed over\n`Finset.range p` so the summand is `z^{k+1}/(k+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}